# the wasm image writer
#
# a linked module is built as a module model from the image record and written
# by the codec's writer. each index space holds the entries the assign phase
# numbered, in index order: an import the image keeps is written from its
# entry's module and field, and a type, table, memory, global or function from
# its input's facts, a function's body as the relocate phase left it. every
# loaded output section that holds bytes is an active data segment at its
# address, zero fill left to the memory's own zeros, and the function table's
# slots are one active element segment from index one. an object's own element
# segment, which lists the functions whose table index it takes, is left out,
# as their relocations make the table. the link's own object names the function
# table, whose size the slots give, the linear memory, whose pages cover the
# loaded data, the global the thread-local block starts at, and the function
# that calls the init functions, whose body the writer builds: a call of every
# init function the image keeps, the lowest priority first and then in input
# order, and a stub for a weak function nothing defines traps. the exports are
# the entry and every export directive, and the target features the settled
# trait. an import whose signature differs from what it reaches is refused, and
# so is an import an image its host runs keeps from a module other than the one
# the host names. the writer writes no debug sections, no name section and no
# producers.

